# Tests that scripts/verify-fast skips. One per line: TARGET NAME, where TARGET
# is `lib` (NAME is the unit test's full path) or a tests/ file stem.
#
# Only slow (about 1 s or more, measured 2026-11-21) media-correctness tests
# belong here. Security, trust, teardown/cancellation, data-preservation,
# overwrite, bounds/budget, cache and paid-request guards always run in the
# fast tier: a slow test that also checks one may be listed only when another
# test that is not listed checks the same guard (for example
# sync_apply existing_output_is_refused_without_overwrite_before_inputs_are_read,
# edit_format subframe_source_end_rounding_is_padded_not_rejected).
# tests/verify_fast_skips.rs rejects names that look like guards, stale names
# and names that would also skip a same-named test elsewhere.
#
# The landing gate is still `cargo test --locked`, which runs all of these.
